				<td width="100%" class="title" colspan="2">I am disappointed...</td>
			</tr>
						<tr>
				<td width="30%" class="body" valign="top">
					<b><div class="smallbody"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/user/view_user.php?id=316">Cebi</a></div></b>
					<div class="xsmall">12/19/2000 - 8:49 PM PST</div>
					<hr width="75%" align="left">
					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=243">Cebi Oathkeeper</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														It seems that I have missed the turmoil that has hit the guild, and was caught<br />
by surprise at the defections.  I am disappointed to see several friends leave the<br />
guild, and more disappointed by the reasons I am hearing.<br />
<br />
Before I joined this guild (at the invite of Coramor), I was almost exclusively a solo<br />
player.  While I did not often group with guild members, I started grouping more often<br />
as a direct result of the social interaction with the guild.  I appreciated the help I<br />
received, and tried to assist where my meager skills allowed.  I liked the basis for<br />
the guild, as it prompted me to read some wonderful literature that I had never been<br />
exposed to.  In sum, This guild added to my enjoyment of Everquest.<br />
<br />
I appreciated the efforts of Lastrae to get this site up and running, and was very<br />
encouraged by the number of people and messages that started appearing here.  The<br />
comaraderie of the guild had gone beyond the game, and was now part of RL (tm).  I<br />
could check the site while I was working (and not actually playing EQ), and was looking<br />
forward to much more in the future.  <br />
<br />
Most of the problems that appear to be afflicting the guild are things that many guilds <br />
go through, but not many survive intact.  The defections from the guild are most likely<br />
not ever going to return, and they will be missed.  The members that are still here now<br />
must make hard choices...is this guild worthwhile and are we willing to work to hold it<br />
together?  That work may mean discussing issues with individuals before assuming the<br />
worst, as misconceptions occur quite often when most communications are a few terse<br />
messages that may not even be seen in the midst of game spam.  It may mean taking<br />
a few minutes to write a message to vent and let others know how you feel.  It may<br />
even mean an apology on occasion.<br />
<br />
I am willing to do what I can to help keep the guild together, I still think that there is <br />
great potential here.  I would like to see us continue to grow, both in numbers and in<br />
community.  I hope (maybe fruitlessly) that former members, like Lastrae, Garlin, Drac and Omyyn, might see the progress and be willing to return one day.  I would also like to see <br />
them welcomed back by the current members.  Ukari, Coramor and other key people,<br />
let your views be known by whatever means you can...your leadership is needed now.<br />
<br />
Sorry for the long winded message,<br />
Cebi Oathkeeper<br />
Monk of the 26th Rank						</td>
